    "result_text": "The full suite is green. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation for the `POST /api/owners` create response (read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`).\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `birthDate` (ISO `date`) input to the `OwnerFields` request schema, and a read-only `ageBand` enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` response schema. The DTOs (`OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnerDto` with `AgeBandEnum`) are generated from this at build time.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with getter/setter, so the value survives between the create and the later GET.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added an `ageBand(Owner)` derivation mapped onto the DTO. It computes whole years via `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate)` and returns `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), or `SENIOR` (\u226565). It returns `null` when either `birthDate` or `registrationDate` is absent, so owners created without a birth date have no age band. MapStruct maps `birthDate` request\u2192entity and entity\u2192response automatically by name.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. h2 is the active profile for tests.\n\nThe new acceptance test (`coreDerivesAgeBand`: birthDate `1990-01-01`, registered today \u2192 `ADULT`) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
